The service already matches the legacy program here, so I changed only the test. `rule_013_order_just_below_50000_through_web_pays_1_00` expected a balance the program never produces.

For that case the legacy computes:
- Order value 49999.99, channel WEB, so commission is 1.00 (`2300-CALCULAR-COMISION`: the value is below 50000).
- `WS-TOTAL` = 49999.99 + 1.00 = 50000.99.
- `PAGODEB` runs `SUBTRACT DEB-MONTO FROM CTA-SALDO`, so the new balance is 60000.00 − 50000.99 = 9999.01.

That is what the service produced, and the OFI variant of the same test (9997.51) already agrees with this arithmetic. The test's 10000.00 is the only wrong expectation, so I changed it to 9999.01. I have not run the tests.

